   "narrative": "As the skirmishers fell back through the gaps in their own lines, Hasdrubal led his heavy horsemen straight at the Roman cavalry along the river. Hemmed in between the water and the infantry, neither side had room to wheel, so the clash turned into a savage standing fight in which many riders dismounted and grappled on foot. Outnumbered nearly three to one, the Roman citizen cavalry was being cut to pieces. On the opposite wing the Numidians rode out against the allied horse and kept it busy, darting in to throw javelins and wheeling away before it could close.",
