   "title": "The cavalry closes the ring",
   "time": "Early afternoon",
   "narrative": "Hasdrubal's horsemen fell on the rear of the legions and completed the ring: Gauls and Spaniards in front, Africans on both flanks, cavalry behind. The Roman army, still more numerous than its enemy, was now trapped on a front of a few hundred metres. Its outer ranks had to fight in every direction while the men inside were crushed together, unable to reach the enemy or to escape, and repeated charges against the rear stopped the mass from turning to break out.",
